{"change_summary":"Clarified the shrimp hatch-rate mineral path with an inline note so spawning's EMA-based mineral handling is not confused with incubation, and stabilized the substrate-redox habitat probe by replacing brittle late-suboxic and inert-decay assertions with stronger outcome checks: planted runs now must show much higher N2 export and materially lower final nitrate than the inert control. I then reformatted and revalidated the touched reproduction and habitat/geometry suites.","outstanding_risks":["Full `tank_harness` package validation is still blocked by unrelated existing compile errors in `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs` (`breeding_success_state` is missing), so only the touched suites were rerun end-to-end.","The redox probe now relies on planted-vs-inert nitrate drawdown and N2-export separation instead of assuming inert denitrifier activity always decays; major redox-model retunes could still require recalibrating the scenario setup."],"steps":[{"description":"Added an inline hatch-rate comment in `shrimp.rs` explaining why incubation still applies `f_mineral` directly while spawning uses the smoothed readiness index.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Reworked the substrate-redox probe assertions and test notes to validate stronger, retuning-resistant denitrification outcomes (`N2` export and final nitrate drawdown) instead of brittle late-suboxic-volume and inert-decay expectations.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Ran formatting plus targeted reproduction and habitat/geometry probe validation, and checked the broader `tank_harness` package to identify the unrelated shrimp-probe compile blocker.","order":3,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo fmt --all` completed successfully.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test reproduction_factors -- --nocapture` passed: 16 tests green, including `test_mineral_suppression_is_applied_once_in_spawning`.","`cargo test -p tank_harness --test e2e_habitat_geometry_probes -- --nocapture` passed: 6 tests green, including `all_habitat_geometry_probes_summary` with 5/5 probes passing.","`all_habitat_geometry_probes_summary` now reports the redox probe passing with strong planted-vs-inert separation: suboxic volume `5042->5746 / 191->0 cm³`, `N2` export `197.93/0.01 mg N`, and activity `0.10->0.67 / 0.10->0.05`.","`cargo test -p tank_harness` still fails before execution because unrelated existing shrimp-probe code references missing `breeding_success_state` in `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs`; this did not affect the touched habitat/geometry suite."]}